invariant: INV-33
file: webpki.c
catches: webpki_auth_test
reason: under pins alone the list framing refuses a Certificate message
  with more than CH_WEBPKI_FLIGHT_ENTRIES entries, the walk's cap, though
  it stores no entry after the leaf. A server that sends a longer chain,
  such as the leaf under eight intermediates of the QUIC Interop Runner's
  amplificationlimit case, fails with bad_certificate although its leaf
  key is pinned. test/webpki_leaf_pins.h's count rows, which want five
  and nine entries accepted, object.

--- old
    while (rb_left(&r) > 0) {
        const uint8_t *cert = NULL;
        size_t cert_len = 0;
--- new
    for (size_t count = 1; rb_left(&r) > 0; count++) {
        const uint8_t *cert = NULL;
        size_t cert_len = 0;
        if (count == CH_WEBPKI_FLIGHT_ENTRIES) {
            return CH_EPROTO; // the walk's cap, though no entry is stored
        }
